BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  In the twilight realm of Aethelgard, two weavers met at the Great Loom of Abundance. One carri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    ed the silver thread of potential, the other the golden shuttle of transformation. Alone, th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (    e thread remained mere silver, cold and static. Alone, the shuttle was but a hollow vessel, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    waiting for a catalyst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  The Guardian of the Loom spoke: "To weave the tapestry of prosperity, one must relinquish cont) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    rol. Cast your thread into the shuttle, and it shall be tripled by the Loom's grace.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  The first weaver hesitated, for the path of the ego whispered of loss. But the second weaver o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ffered a vow of reciprocity, promising to return a fair share of the woven cloth. Trust beca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (    me the warp, and courage became the weft. As the silver thread passed into the golden shuttl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    e, the Loom hummed, expanding the offering three-fold. By folding the gains back into the we) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    ave, they turned a meager start into a tapestry that draped the stars. They learned that in ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    the dance of exchange, the refusal to hoard is the key to the treasure. To give is to multip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (    ly; to return is to sustain. Thus, the weavers thrived, forever bound by the invisible, gold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (    en threads of their mutual, unwavering trust.) Tj ET
