BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  In the beginning, the Weaver held five seeds of silver. She could keep them, locked in her iro) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    n fist, or cast them into the fertile void. She chose to cast them. As they fell, a cosmic w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    ind-the multiplier of the gods-tripled their count. The Gardener caught the fifteen golden g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (    rains, his palms cupped in expectation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  Greed is a hungry ghost, whispering of hidden caches and solitary wealth. But the Gardener kne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    w the ancient law of the scales: what is given must be returned, or the cycle breaks. He pla) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    nted the seeds, nurtured them with his own essence, and harvested their fruit. From the fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    een, he kept a portion for his labor but returned a generous sum to the Weaver's outstretche) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    d hand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  The Weaver's store swelled; the Gardener's soil thrived. They played this dance through eons, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    two souls tethered by the golden thread of trust. When a hand offered, a hand accepted, and ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    a hand returned, the stars burned brighter. But when a heart hardened, fearing loss, the gar) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    den turned to ash. For the universe does not reward the hoarder, but the one who understands) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (     that to hold everything is, in the end, to possess nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
