BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  In the beginning, the world of Aethel was a vast, arid expanse of grey stone. Two travelers, F) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (    inn and his companion, stood before a single, shimmering seed. Finn held the seed, knowing t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    hat if he buried it in the dust, the gods would multiply its essence threefold. Yet, he hesi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    tated, fearing the sun-baked earth might swallow his offering whole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  "Plant it," his companion whispered. "The soil yields only to those who dare.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  Finn planted the seed. As promised, the earth bloomed into an orchard of golden fruit, far ric) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    her than the original gift. The companion stood among the branches, the weight of the harves) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    t heavy in her hands. She saw the fear in Finn's eyes-the fear of abandonment. She understoo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (    d that if she took all, the orchard would wither, and the next season would bring only droug) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (    ht and solitude. She reached out, dividing the golden bounty equally, returning a generous p) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ortion to Finn.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  The cycle continued, season after season, as the orchard grew into an endless forest. They lea) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    rned that the earth did not reward the greedy, nor the fearful. It rewarded the bridge-the s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    hared harvest that bound them together, turning a barren wasteland into a paradise of consta) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    nt, mutual prosperity.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  **Crafting a Trusting Myth**) Tj ET
