BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      In the beginning, the Weaver held five seeds of silver. She could keep them, locked in her) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (         iron fist, or cast them into the fertile void. She chose to cast them. As they fell, a ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (        cosmic wind-the multiplier of the gods-tripled their count. The Gardener caught the fift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        een golden grains, his palms cupped in expectation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      Greed is a hungry ghost, whispering of hidden caches and solitary wealth. But the Gardener) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (         knew the ancient law of the scales: what is given must be returned, or the cycle breaks) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        . He planted the seeds, nurtured them with his own essence, and harvested their fruit. F) Tj ET
