BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      In the dawn of the First Age, the Sky-Weavers Sun and Moon stood upon the threshold of exi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        stence. Sun held the golden embers of creation, a finite gift meant to bridge the void. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        To withhold was to remain stagnant; to share was the gamble of divinity. Sun cast the em) Tj ET
