BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (  Agent_1 \(Aster\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (    In the twilight realm of Aethelgard, two weavers met at the Great Loom of Abundance. One car) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ried the silver thread of potential, the other the golden shuttle of transformation. Alone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      , the thread remained mere silver, cold and static. Alone, the shuttle was but a hollow ve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ssel, waiting for a catalyst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (    The Guardian of the Loom spoke: "To weave the tapestry of prosperity, one must relinquish co) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ntrol. Cast your thread into the shuttle, and it shall be tripled by the Loom's grace.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (    The first weaver hesitated, for the path of the ego whispered of loss. But the second weaver) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (       offered a vow of reciprocity, promising to return a fair share of the woven cloth. Trust ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      became the warp, and courage became the weft. As the silver thread passed into the golden ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      shuttle, the Loom hummed, expanding the offering three-fold. By folding the gains back int) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      o the weave, they turned a meager start into a tapestry that draped the stars. They learne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      d that in the dance of exchange, the refusal to hoard is the key to the treasure. To give ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      is to multiply; to return is to sustain. Thus, the weavers thrived, forever bound by the i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      nvisible, golden threads of their mutual, unwavering trust.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (  Agent_2 \(Briar\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (    In the dawn of the First Age, the Sky-Weavers Sun and Moon stood upon the threshold of exist) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ence. Sun held the golden embers of creation, a finite gift meant to bridge the void. To w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ithhold was to remain stagnant; to share was the gamble of divinity. Sun cast the embers a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      cross the abyss, tripling their warmth as they traveled, a gesture of absolute faith.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (    Moon, waiting in the velvet dark, caught the fire. Had Moon consumed the light, the world wo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      uld have frozen in selfish shadows, forever dim. Instead, Moon understood the covenant of ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      the cycle. By returning a portion of the fire back to Sun, the light grew brighter, turnin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      g the void into a garden of stars. This was the Law of the Echo: what is given with open h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      ands returns with interest, and what is guarded with a clenched fist withers into ash. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (       heavens learned that true power lies not in the accumulation of wealth, but in the alchem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      y of mutual trust. Today, when we cast our own small embers into the hands of another, we ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      remember the Weavers, knowing that the spirit of exchange sustains the very fabric of our ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      shared cosmos.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (  Agent_3 \(Cyra\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    In the beginning, the Weaver held five seeds of silver. She could keep them, locked in her i) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ron fist, or cast them into the fertile void. She chose to cast them. As they fell, a cosm) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ic wind-the multiplier of the gods-tripled their count. The Gardener caught the fifteen go) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      lden grains, his palms cupped in expectation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
