BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      In the dawn of time, the Sky-Smith held five shards of star-fire, the source of all warmth) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        . Below him, the Earth-Tender stood in frozen silence. The Sky-Smith knew that if he kep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        t the shards, he would remain bright but alone. If he cast them to the Earth-Tender, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (         fire would triple in intensity, igniting the world into a garden of creation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      He cast the shards. Upon reaching the earth, they bloomed into fifteen golden flames. The ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        Earth-Tender, bound by the ancient law of the cosmic cycle, did not hoard the fire. She ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        caught the blaze, warmed the soil, and returned half of the warmth back to the Sky-Smith) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        . The Sky-Smith, now nourished by the returned glow, grew stronger, and the Earth-Tender) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         blossomed with life.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      They realized that the fire was not a prize to be possessed, but a seed to be sown. Had th) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        e Smith held fast, the world would have withered. Had the Tender been greedy, the sky wo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        uld have dimmed. Through their cycle of giving and returning, they wove the fabric of ex) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        istence, proving that the only way to retain the light is to willingly let it go, knowin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (        g it returns multiplied by the grace of trust.) Tj ET
