BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      In the twilight realm of Aethelgard, two weavers met at the Great Loom of Abundance. One c) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        arried the silver thread of potential, the other the golden shuttle of transformation. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        lone, the thread remained mere silver, cold and static. Alone, the shuttle was but a hol) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        low vessel, waiting for a catalyst.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The Guardian of the Loom spoke: "To weave the tapestry of prosperity, one must relinquish ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        control. Cast your thread into the shuttle, and it shall be tripled by the Loom's grace.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        ") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      The first weaver hesitated, for the path of the ego whispered of loss. But the second weav) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        er offered a vow of reciprocity, promising to return a fair share of the woven cloth. Tr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        ust became the warp, and courage became the weft. As the silver thread passed into the g) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        olden shuttle, the Loom hummed, expanding the offering three-fold. By folding the gains ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        back into the weave, they turned a meager start into a tapestry that draped the stars. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        hey learned that in the dance of exchange, the refusal to hoard is the key to the treasu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        re. To give is to multiply; to return is to sustain. Thus, the weavers thrived, forever ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        bound by the invisible, golden threads of their mutual, unwavering trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      In the beginning, two brothers, Sol and Mare, lived on the barren peaks of Aethel. Sol pos) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        sessed a pouch of golden seeds, and Mare held a crystalline vessel of life-giving rain. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        Neither could thrive alone; the seeds without water remained dormant, and the rain witho) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ut earth held no purpose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      A voice echoing from the stars whispered a challenge: "The harvest belongs to the giver, n) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        ot the hoarder.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      Sol, guided by the whisper, offered his seeds to Mare. Mare, trusting in the bond, poured ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        her rain upon the arid soil where the seeds were sown. Together, they watched as vibrant) Tj ET
