BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (         the return of these golden stones. If a stone was kept entirely on one side, the river ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        would grow stagnant and dim, its magic fading into the mud. When a traveler from one sid) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        e tossed their offering, they were not losing their wealth, but launching an act of fait) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (        h into the deep. Those on the opposite bank understood that their duty was to mirror tha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        t grace, returning a portion that kept the flow balanced and vibrant. This was the dance) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         of the tide: a constant, rhythmic oscillation of generosity that allowed both villages ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        to flourish in perpetual abundance. They learned that the river was not a divider, but a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (         conduit for shared prosperity. By choosing to sustain the cycle rather than hoard the t) Tj ET
